---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import InfoCard from '../../components/InfoCard.astro';
import { SITE, u } from '../../config';
import media from '../../data/media.json';
const m = media as any;
const ph = m.photos.portrait;
---
<Base title="About">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1 class="display">ABOUT</h1>
    <div class="about__intro">
      <figure class="portrait">
        <a href={u(ph.src)} data-lb data-lb-group="about" data-lb-round="1" data-lb-src={u(ph.src)} data-lb-alt={ph.alt} data-lb-title="Aritra Mitra at the Jindal School of Art and Architecture" data-lb-meta="About">
          <img class="round" src={u(ph.sm)} srcset={`${u(ph.sm)} 320w, ${u(ph.src)} 800w`} sizes="(min-width: 640px) 220px, 160px" alt={ph.alt} width="220" height="220" />
        </a>
        <figcaption class="label label--indigo">JINDAL SCHOOL OF ART &amp; ARCHITECTURE</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p>I'm Aritra, a third-year BDes student in Immersive Digital Environments at O.P. Jindal Global University, designing games and spaces people can step into.</p>
        <p>I like to start with a question, then research, prototype, get critiqued and iterate. Tiger Run grew out of a Grade 10 drawing about wildlife conservation. SoleSync began with a trust problem in buying sneakers and ended as a prototype I critiqued three times. My environment and lighting work comes from studying how real light behaves, then rebuilding it in Maya and Unreal Engine.</p>
        <p>I'm looking for an internship in game design, immersive environments or UX, where I can learn fast and contribute to real production work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="h2">More about me</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <InfoCard label="PLAYER STATS" title="Areas + tools" sprite="hero">
        <p><strong>Areas:</strong> game + environment, UX + systems, motion + lighting.</p>
        <p><strong>Tools:</strong> Maya · SketchUp · Unreal Engine · Figma · Google Stitch · Procreate · Blender (basic) · AutoCAD (basic)</p>
      </InfoCard>
      <InfoCard href={u('/work/doom-and-quake/')} label="THE ORIGIN" title="Where the look comes from" img={u(m['doom-and-quake'].thumb)} imgAlt={m['doom-and-quake'].heroAlt} cta="READ THE WHOLE REPORT →">
        <p>I presented my Doom and Quake report as an arcade title screen, and the pixel-arcade look stuck. It became the identity of this site and my printed card.</p>
      </InfoCard>
      <InfoCard href={SITE.instagramFeatured} external label="WILDLIFE PHOTOGRAPHY" title="@wildscapeexplorers" sprite="tiger" cta="SEE THE FIRST POST →">
        <p>I photograph wildlife, the same concern for animals and habitat that sits behind Tiger Run.</p>
      </InfoCard>
      <InfoCard href={u('/resume/')} label="RÉSUMÉ" title="Preview + download" img={u('/img/resume-preview.webp')} imgAlt="First page of Aritra Mitra's résumé" cta="OPEN THE RÉSUMÉ →">
        <p>One page: profile, highlights, toolbox and selected projects.</p>
      </InfoCard>
      <InfoCard href={u('/contact/')} label="CONTACT" title="Say hello" sprite="star" cta="GET IN TOUCH →">
        <p>Email, LinkedIn and Instagram. Open to internships in game design, immersive environments and UX.</p>
      </InfoCard>
      <InfoCard id="build" variant="pink" label="BUILD NOTE" title="How this site was made" sprite="heart">
        <p>This website was <strong>coded with Claude</strong>, an AI assistant from Anthropic. Claude is the enabler: it wrote the code.</p>
        <p>The strategy, information architecture, arcade design system, choice of work and the full specification are <strong>Aritra Mitra's</strong>.</p>
        <p class="muted">SoleSync research data is simulated for coursework.</p>
      </InfoCard>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
